      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Lavastorm Mountains 3.0 [zone=31]\n**Who:**\n- Captain Areha Burina [npc=17807]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 70\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Faction\n- Loot\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Faction Required:**\nNorrath's Keepers (Min: Warmly)\n**Related Zones:**\n- Accursed Nest: In the Shadows [zone=375]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Vishimtar the Fallen [npc=17716]\n- a chest - In the Shadows [npc=23792]\n- a spirit wraith [npc=21407]\n- cloud of concentrated chaos [npc=21411]\n- corrupted drake [npc=21409]\n- incorporeal shadow [npc=21353]\n- lifedrain shadow [npc=21408]\n- mournful spirit [npc=21410]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Dragons of Norrath Progression (Norrath's Keepers) [quest=3061]\n**Era:** | !Dragons of Norrath\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Raid\n**Min. # of Players:** | 6\n**Max. # of Players:** | 54\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Sun Mar 13 21:05:56 2005\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 |\n---\n\n**For an overview of the Dragons of Norrath expansion, see this wiki article.**\n**For an overview of progression, see quest entries for Norrath's Keepers [quest=3061] and the Dark Reign [quest=3062].**\n\n---\n\n_This raid task begins with Captain Areha Burina ( **click for map image**) in the Norrath's Keepers camp of the Lavastorm Mountains._\n_Pre-requisites for requesting this task:_\n\\- Minimum 6 players; maximum 54 players\n\\- Must be warmly faction with Norrath's Keepers\n\\- Completion of all Tier 4 tasks and flags (including the raids)\n\\- Completion of \"Origins of the Curse\" (group mission)\n\\- Completion of \"The Curse of Ju`rek\" (raid)\nYou say, 'Hail, Captain Areha Burina'\nCaptain Areha Burina bows. 'I see a good heart in you and a measure of bravery. Serve Firiona Vie and Norrath's Keepers well!'\nYou have been assigned the task 'In the Shadows'.\nTerrible events came to pass as Yar`Lir was taken from her perch. There was a dragon that protected the Nest beneath the islands in the sky, but now that place has turned to ruin and darkness. After seeing the effects the corruption has caused the Nest, we can only guess what has happened to the dragon that inhabited it. Go now and be swift. If this dragon is a plague on our lands, it must be stopped.\n\n---\n\n**Task Steps**\nTouch the portal to The Nest 0/1 (The Broodlands)\nConfront Vishimtar the Fallen 0/1 (The Accursed Nest)\n**TASK LOCKS HERE**\nKill Vishimtar the Fallen 0/1 (The Accursed Nest)\n\n---\n\n**The Event**\n_In this raid instance, you will find a formidable foe: Vishimtar the Fallen, who comes with numerous adds and tricks. Vishimtar hits for a max ~4,500; AE rampages (mitigated to ~1,000 per hit); and casts \"Vishimtar's Shadow\", \"Vishimtar's Aura\", and \"Withering Corruption\" throughout the event:_\nVishimtar the Fallen says 'The nest, the children... must be protected.'\nVishimtar's Shadow: PB AE 2000', Chromatic (-500)\n1: Decrease HP when cast by 1250\n2: Decrease Hitpoints by 850 per tick\n4: Decrease Movement by 5%\n11: Decrease Mana by 5 per tick\nVishimtar's Aura: Self 0', Magic (0)\n1: Increase Damage Shield by 15\n2: Increase Spell-Damage Shield by 250\nWithering Corruption: Single Target, Magic (-1000)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 100 per tick\n2: Cast Upon Fade: Vishimtar's Corruption\nVishimtar's Corruption: Self 0', Magic (-1000)\n1: Decrease AC by 600\n2: Max HP change by (-75%)\n3: Decrease Agro Multiplier by 95%\n_At about 75% health, 4x \"incorporeal shadow\" spawn. These don't hit hard at all and have relatively few hitpoints. If killed, a \"lifedrain shadow\" spawns in its place. The lifedrain shadows hit for a max ~2,000 and flurry, so you want to avoid killing the incorporeal shadows if you can._\n_3-6 minutes after Vishimtar is initially aggro'd and every 75-120 seconds thereafter, a \"tainted egg\" spawns at a random location. If these aren't killed within a few moments of spawning (blunt-weapons only), multiple mobs called \"a corrupted drakeling\" spawn from it and attack. These hit for a max ~1,200 and flurry._\n_At 50% health, the four \"corrupted drake\" mobs around the room go aggro. These are snareable and, if killed, immediately respawn._\n_At 25% health, Vishimtar locks health and starts casting \"Creeping Doom\" on random targets (45-second intervals, maximum four targets at a time). This spell must be cured before it fades (48 seconds), otherwise the inflicted player is death touched. To cure this, go to one of the \"mournful spirit\" dervishes that roam around the perimeter of the event area and say \"shoulder my burden\" to it:_\nYou say, 'Hail, mournful spirit'\nAn otherworldly voice rings in your mind, 'I can sense that you have been afflicted by Vishimtar, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. You will not survive long - soon death will take you and corrupt your body into a twisted shell of hatred. Allow me to help you. I can [shoulder your burden].'\nYou say, 'Shoulder my burden'\nThe mournful spirit draws corruption from your body and absorbs it, destroying itself in the process.\nmournful spirit died.\n_For each cure of \"Creeping Doom\", Vishimtar's health unlocks 1%._\nCreeping Doom: Single Target, Unresistable (-1000)\n1: Decrease Stats by 120\n2: Cast Upon Fade: Creeping Doom Trigger\n_If anyone dies or goes linkdead at any time in the event, \"a spirit wraith\" spawns in their place. These skeletons hit for a max ~1,500; have zonewide aggro; and are mezzable (note: pet deaths don't spawn adds)._\n_Note: Throughout the event, you'll sometimes get a \"cloud of concentrated chaos\" spawn. You can kill these to fill up everyone's health and mana._\n\n---\n\n**Completion & Loot**\n_Kill Vishimtar to complete the task:_\nVishimtar the Fallen has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nVishimtar crumples. His corrupted form no longer casts shadows upon the cavern walls.\nYour faction standing with Vishimtar has been adjusted by -1.\nYour faction standing with Cursed Drakes has been adjusted by -1.\nVishimtar's feeble attempts to protect the Nest were no match for your prowess.\n_Following Vishimtar's death, all adds despawn and a chest spawns with loot. Vishimtar himself drops 9x \"Shadowscale of Vishimtar\" (Tier 5 progression item) + 1x \"Eye of Vishimtar\" (turn-in item for **a mask** [quest=3090])._\n_The chest contains 3 items from this loot table:_\nAccursed Earhoop of Pain\nBelt of the Black Dragon\nCloak of Deepshadow\nCord of the Cunning\nDark Heart of Vishimtar\nDragonkiller\nFace of Unfeeling\nMottled Black Dragonscale\nObsidian Pauldrons\nRod of Shaded Wrath\nSkull of Vishimtar\n_Task Rewards:_\n9x \"Radiant Crystal\"\n1x \"Norrath's Keepers Token\" (faction **turn-in** [quest=3134] item)\n_Note: If doing this raid as part of progression, you'll want to check in with some NPCs to make sure your flags are up to date. See **this quest entry** [quest=3061] for more details._\n**Submitted by:** Saraban of Darkwind\n- Accursed Earhoop of Pain [item=34904]\n- Belt of the Black Dragon [item=34903]\n- Cloak of Deepshadow [item=34901]\n- Dark Heart of Vishimtar [item=34905]\n- Dragonkiller [item=35002]\n- Face of Unfeeling [item=35004]\n- Mottled Black Dragonscale [item=35003]\n- Norrath's Keepers Token [item=34991]\n- Obsidian Pauldrons [item=35206]\n- Radiant Crystal [item=34988]\n- Rod of Shaded Wrath [item=34902]\n- Shadowscale of Vishimtar [item=35001]\n- Skull of Vishimtar [item=35000]",
